### name: textif.sqlite.dedupe
--- dialect
sqlite
--- bindings
{"R": {"kind": "relation", "from": "r", "fields": {"N": {"kind": "column", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}, "T": {"kind": "column", "column": "t", "type": "TEXT"}}}}
--- as
statement
--- source
R .> MAP(RECORD("s", IF(_["n"] > 1, "a", "b"))) .> DEDUPE()
--- expect
SELECT DISTINCT CAST(CASE WHEN (CAST("n" AS NUMERIC) > CAST('1' AS NUMERIC)) THEN 'a' ELSE 'b' END AS TEXT) COLLATE BINARY AS "s" FROM "r"
===

### name: textif.sqlite.cond
--- dialect
sqlite
--- bindings
{"R": {"kind": "relation", "from": "r", "fields": {"N": {"kind": "column", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}, "T": {"kind": "column", "column": "t", "type": "TEXT"}}}}
--- as
statement
--- source
R .> MAP(RECORD("s", COND(_["n"] > 1, "a", _["n"] > 0, "b", "c"))) .> DEDUPE()
--- expect
SELECT DISTINCT CAST(CASE WHEN (CAST("n" AS NUMERIC) > CAST('1' AS NUMERIC)) THEN 'a' WHEN (CAST("n" AS NUMERIC) > CAST('0' AS NUMERIC)) THEN 'b' ELSE 'c' END AS TEXT) COLLATE BINARY AS "s" FROM "r"
===

### name: textif.postgresql.nested
--- note
A result that is itself a conditional of text literals is one of them too.
--- dialect
postgresql
--- bindings
{"R": {"kind": "relation", "from": "r", "fields": {"N": {"kind": "column", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}, "T": {"kind": "column", "column": "t", "type": "TEXT"}}}}
--- as
statement
--- source
R .> MAP(RECORD("s", IF(_["n"] > 1, "a", IF(_["n"] > 0, "b", "c")))) .> DEDUPE()
--- expect
SELECT DISTINCT CAST(CASE WHEN ("n" > 1) THEN 'a' ELSE CASE WHEN ("n" > 0) THEN 'b' ELSE 'c' END END AS TEXT) COLLATE "C" AS "s" FROM "r"
===

### name: textif.postgresql.no-else
--- note
A two-argument IF gives "" otherwise (§7.2): a text literal too.
--- dialect
postgresql
--- bindings
{"R": {"kind": "relation", "from": "r", "fields": {"N": {"kind": "column", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}, "T": {"kind": "column", "column": "t", "type": "TEXT"}}}}
--- as
statement
--- source
R .> MAP(RECORD("s", IF(_["n"] > 1, "a"))) .> DEDUPE()
--- expect
SELECT DISTINCT CAST(CASE WHEN ("n" > 1) THEN 'a' ELSE '' END AS TEXT) COLLATE "C" AS "s" FROM "r"
===

### name: plan.textif.mariadb.bucket-after-a-map-splits-at-the-map
--- note
The barrier lets the MAP end a prefix. The BUCKET stays in memory: a derived
table types a computed column UNKNOWN, and a group key must be typed.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"R": {"kind": "relation", "from": "r", "fields": {"N": {"kind": "column", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}, "T": {"kind": "column", "column": "t", "type": "TEXT"}}}}
--- source
R .> MAP(RECORD("s", IF(_["n"] > 1, "a", "b"))) .> BUCKET(_["s"], RECORD("k", _K, "c", COUNT(_)))
--- plan
hybrid
--- tables
r
--- expect
SELECT CASE WHEN (`n` > 1) THEN 'a' ELSE 'b' END AS `s` FROM `r`
===

### name: plan.textif.postgresql.dedupe-is-one-statement
--- dialect
postgresql
--- bindings
{"R": {"kind": "relation", "from": "r", "fields": {"N": {"kind": "column", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}, "T": {"kind": "column", "column": "t", "type": "TEXT"}}}}
--- source
R .> MAP(RECORD("s", IF(_["n"] > 1, "a", "b"))) .> DEDUPE()
--- plan
pure_sql
--- tables
r
--- expect
SELECT DISTINCT CAST(CASE WHEN ("n" > 1) THEN 'a' ELSE 'b' END AS TEXT) COLLATE "C" AS "s" FROM "r"
===

### name: plan.textif.postgresql.numeric-results-stay-local
--- dialect
postgresql
--- bindings
{"R": {"kind": "relation", "from": "r", "fields": {"N": {"kind": "column", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}, "T": {"kind": "column", "column": "t", "type": "TEXT"}}}}
--- source
R .> MAP(RECORD("s", IF(_["n"] > 1, 1, 1.0))) .> DEDUPE()
--- plan
pure_memory
--- tables
r
===

### name: plan.textif.postgresql.a-column-result-stays-local
--- note
The rule is about literals; a column read in a branch is not one.
--- dialect
postgresql
--- bindings
{"R": {"kind": "relation", "from": "r", "fields": {"N": {"kind": "column", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}, "T": {"kind": "column", "column": "t", "type": "TEXT"}}}}
--- source
R .> MAP(RECORD("s", IF(_["n"] > 1, "a", _["t"]))) .> DEDUPE()
--- plan
pure_memory
--- tables
r
===

